                        Suffolk. Benedictine abbey of St Edmund, King and Martyr.
                        </orgName><p>'Liber monachorum S. Edmundi in quo continentur. . .' . B.231.
                        (on flyleaf).</p><p>There are notes by Robert Grosseteste at fol. 1v
                        recording an exchange of books: 'Memoriale magistri Roberti Grossetes' pro
                        Exameron Basilii'. The text of this present book which Grosseteste offered
                        in the exchange consists of reportationes from Paris lectures on the Gloss
                        (see A. Gransden, A History of the Abbey of Bury St Edmunds, 1257--1301
                        (2015), 273, citing B. Smalley in Cambridge Historical Journal 6 (1938),
                        103--4).</p><q type="pressmark">B.231</q></provenance>
